<title>ISRAEL: Israel foreign reserves reach record $16.4 billion.</title>
<headline>Israel foreign reserves reach record $16.4 billion.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves at the end of May rose to a record $16.394 billion, the Bank of Israel said on Sunday.</p>
<p>			(in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>		  May 1997     April 1997     May 1996</p>
<p>Reserves	 16,394	  16,011	   9,252</p>
<p>The central bank said the increase was due to continued foreign currency borrowing by the private sector and to foreign investment.</p>
<p>It added that reserves grew more slowly in May than in any of the previous three months because of a considerably smaller increase in forex borrowing.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 x233</p>
</text>
